.TH XD\-CONTROL 1 2026-10-18 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xd\-control \- open Control Panel or one of its applets
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY xd\-control
.RI [ applet ]
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
Without an argument,
.B xd\-control
opens the Control Panel folder
.RB ( control:///
in
.BR xd\-files (1)),
in Windows XP's Category View or Classic View.
.PP
With one, it opens that applet, as Windows'
.B control desk.cpl
does.
.I applet
may be the program's name with or without
.B xd\-
.RB ( desk ", " xd\-desk ),
with
.B .cpl
.RB ( desk.cpl ),
the desktop entry's id or its name
.RB ( Display ),
in any case.
.PP
An applet is any installed desktop entry with
.B X\-XeonDesktop\-ControlPanel
in its
.BR Categories ;
its
.B X\-XeonDesktop\-ControlPanel\-Category
key
.RB ( appearance ", " network ", " programs ", " sound ", " performance ,
.BR hardware ", " accounts ", " datetime " or " accessibility )
files it in Category View.
.PP
XeonDesktop's applets:
.BR xd\-access (1),
.BR xd\-admintools (1),
.BR xd\-appwiz (1),
.BR xd\-bluetooth (1),
.BR xd\-desk (1),
.BR xd\-folders (1),
.BR xd\-fonts (1),
.BR xd\-intl (1),
.BR xd\-joy (1),
.BR xd\-keyboard (1),
.BR xd\-mouse (1),
.BR xd\-netconn (1),
.BR xd\-power (1),
.BR xd\-printers (1),
.BR xd\-scanners (1),
.BR xd\-schedtasks (1),
.BR xd\-sound (1),
.BR xd\-sysdm (1),
.BR xd\-taskbar (1),
.BR xd\-timedate (1)
and
.BR xd\-users (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a summary and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
1 when there is no such applet or it can't be started.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xd\-files (1)
